Z||000004||TOM||09-25-1999||11:06 AM||||I've done the ported manifolds. The headlight mod which I really like. The rear deck lid scoop. Im working on a holley style scoop. I've added all the options. Not that they are mods. I think thats it. I would do a short shifter but mine is an auto.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-20-1999||03:10 AM||||Why coldn't you do a short shifter on an auto?  Making a custom dash and having some clearance probs with shifter.  Don't know exactly how I'm gonna do it, but I'll be taking about 1 1/2" off of my shifter.  Also, why not use a different shifter knob for a different look?  Took one out of my wifes '98 Cavalier.  Not a major mod, but little things count, too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierosound||11-21-1999||07:57 PM||||The best information I've come across so far is here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.users.uswest.net/~racing2win/mild2wld.htm#2800V6misc" TARGET=_blank>www.users.uswest.net/~racing2win/mild2wld.htm#2800V6misc</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||11-21-1999||10:20 PM||||Let ME be the first to start prattling off my mods. I did it all myself so I have just a touch of pride when I list it.<P>85 Fiero GT (Black)<P>Block:<BR>Stress relieved (removed all casting flash and edges.)<BR>Painted bright red<P>Heads:<BR>Ported,<BR>polished, <BR>valve job (3 angle cut)<BR>Roller tip rockers 1:6<BR>Babe Erson Cam - 444 lift 260 duration (LOVE that cam sound!)<P>Suspension:<BR>Urethane bushings-<BR>-Torque strut<BR>-Engine Cradle<BR>-Front Control Arms<BR>-Rear control Arms<BR>-Front Sway Bar<P><BR>General:<BR>-Match ported intake, exhaust<BR>-Triple Chromed/Polished various parts and brackets.<BR>-Took the flash off of the intake plenum and powder coated red.<BR>-Cross drilled rear rotors (fronts coming soon)<BR>-Front/Rear bumpers from 88 Formula/Coupe<BR>-Image Eclipse 16 x 7 wheels w Aurora 225/50/16<BR>-Manual Fan Switch (love it in traffic!)<BR>-Short Shifter with Leather Camaro knob (Looks great!)<P>Coming Attractions:<P>-2 1/2 inch exhaust w Megs Tips<BR>-Rear Sway Bar<BR>-BF Goodrich Comp TA VR4s (Had them on before, couldn't find them. Found them after I bought these tires! Argh!)<BR>-Lowering down to an acceptable height (NOT the bumpstops!)<BR>-Stereo that works!<BR>-Interior that doesn't look lived in<P>uhhhhhhh I think thats it...||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||11-21-1999||10:33 PM||||P.S. All that work a year or 2 before we started putting in the 3.4s! Argh! Ran out of money for the headers and the 3.1 crank! Argh again!!! But got a lot of nice pictures...||||reg||1
Z||000009||superXmotorsports||11-21-1999||10:37 PM||||WKDFIRO you forgot to mention what clutch you're using to put down all that power...||||reg||3
Z||000010||superXmotorsports||11-21-1999||10:53 PM||||Last 87 GT:<BR>3.2 stroker<BR>HKS super power flow intake<BR>muffler-eliminator exhaust w/ 4.5" megs tips<BR>ASP underdrive pulley<BR>Hypertech powerstat, c-fan switch, stage II<BR>Crane compucam<BR>adjustable fuel pressure regulator<BR>all poly bushings + dogbone<BR>heavy duty front+rear sway bars<BR>16 x 8 SWR revolution triple chrome wheels<P>new 87 GT project:<P>3.2 stroker balanced/blueprinted<BR>10.5:1 Venola forged pistons<BR>Crane cam, steel crank, tricked heads<BR>full length headers<BR>4" exhaust w/ flowmaster muffler (to be replaced by a titanium unit)<BR>Corvette TPI w/ SUPERCHIPS custom CPU<BR>custom PRM intake / ramair<BR>aluminum cradle bushings<BR>poly suspension bushings/dogbone<BR>KONI shocks/struts<BR>lowering springs, front/rear sway bars<BR>strut tower brace, X-frame reinforcement<BR>SS brake lines, cross-drilled rotors w/ painted calipers<BR>17 X 7 front, 17 X 9 rear Team Loco 150 chrome wheels w/ Yokohama A032R autocross tires<BR>Sparco racing seats<P>by spring:<BR>50hp NOS<BR>Cliff's digital gauges  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>cut off the roof!!<BR>Firebird mirrors<BR>Fly yellow monochrome paint<P>||||reg||1
