Z||000014||superXmotorsports||11-22-1999||09:39 AM||||I have to locate a pair (4th gen) first to be sure.  You will have to fill in the 3 holes in the door skin left by the factory mirrors.  The Fbird mirrors should attach in that corner area of the door like they do on the bird.  I will add the pics of my new project to my site as I get them. <A HREF="http://users.desupernet.com/superx" TARGET=_blank>http://users.desupernet.com/superx</A> <BR>||||reg||14
Z||000015||Monkeyman||11-22-1999||08:32 PM||||superX--how do you fill in plastic body panels?  The same as you would if it were fiberglass?  I was thinking about body mounted mirrors myself, but didn't know how.||||reg||5
Z||000016||superXmotorsports||11-22-1999||09:45 PM||||I am not a body-man myself but the area behind the holes in the door skin will be reinforced/covered and then filled in with whatever the shop feels is appropriate.  I have bought several Fieros over the years that had the luggage rack removed and filled in the holes and they never looked very good - however they were never reinforced from behind either.  I will keep those who are interested updated and will send the info to Tom who seems to be a Fiero fabrication pro...||||reg||3
Z||000017||batboy||11-22-1999||09:57 PM||||Batmobile: Silver 1985 Fiero SE<P>Chevy 350 V8 (4 bolt mains)<BR>Tilton high torque starter<BR>Edelbrock Performer 4 barrel carb<BR>Edelbrock Pro Flo air cleaner<BR>Custom dual exhaust system<BR>3" Hooker chrome resonator tips<BR>Prothane control arm bushings<BR>Energy Suspension sway bar bushings/end links<BR>Suspension Techniques lower front springs<BR>Grand Am brake swap (front and rear)<BR>New Moog ball joints and tie rods<BR>small side air scoop (brand unknown)<BR>added optional factory ralley gauge pod<BR>Auto Meter Sport electric speedo and tach<BR>Pioneer DEH-45DH CD player<BR>Pioneer 4"X10" front speakers<BR>Rockford-Fosgate Punch amp and 8" subwoofer<BR>Front battery mounting kit (not yet installed)<P>Future mods: rear sway bar<BR>front hood louvers (1986 Trans Am?)<BR>DGP stage 1 body kit (air dam, ground effects,<BR>and rear wrap around spoiler)||||reg||1
Z||000018||WKDFIRO||11-23-1999||12:34 AM||||Sorry about that, <BR>Its a 4 speed. A good friend of mine (who has an awesome yellow 88 GT) cut it and rewelded it. And the name of the clutch I use......<P>Mcleod.<P>Its a little larger in diameter than stock.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Monkeyman||11-26-1999||08:50 PM||||Called my local bodyshop today.  They said that you can fill in the mirror hole in the door by fiberglassing both sides and make sure you put something in the hole for support (a cut to fit piece of plastic?).  Here's another idea.  A friend of mine works in a prototype shop in the metal fab shop I work at.  He has a plastic welder (I swear!).  He said that basically it is a heat gun with a strand of wire.  Supposed to work like a MIG (?) welder, but for plastic.  Haven't seen it in operation yet, nor do I know the cost of one, but it seems like it would be worth some money.  Think of all of the neat things you could do with one.  If you had a crack in a fascia, you could fix it easily.  I'll check on the price and limitations and get back.||||reg||7
