Z||000029||SCCA FIERO||11-28-1999||06:01 PM||||I bought a tired 4 cylinder 88 Fiero and already had a strong running 86 SE V6 with frame damage. Result:<P>1988 Coupe 5 spd Isuzu tranny.<BR>added a set of 87GT wheels with the inset painted black.<BR>spoiler from my 86,<BR>120 mph speedo,<BR>chopped the shifter,<BR>poly dogbone bushings,<BR>Holley scoop (soon mecham scoops),<BR>dash from my 86 SE,<BR>power windows,<BR>power locks,<BR>cruise control,<BR>OH... and a 2.8 V6  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Coming soon:<BR>sunroof.... maybe, I have all the parts but not sure if I want to do it anymore. kinda like the hardtop look.<BR>Fastback conversion.... got the parts<BR>Turbo ...have the turbo and Y pipe... just no time<BR>fresh paint <BR>poly suspension<BR>rear swaybar<BR>the list is endless....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000030||superXmotorsports||11-28-1999||08:00 PM||||SCCA - the beauty of your V6/Isuzu 5 spd combo is that you can change the gears or final drive ratio of your tranny.  The Isuzuperformance site offers alot of options for that 5 spd.  They have 4.10's etc.||||reg||3
Z||000031||WKDFIRO||11-28-1999||08:52 PM||||Speaking of 4.10s. The 84 Sport Coupe and SE 4 spd manual had 4.10 gears. This final gear has been successfully been taken out of the 84 case (case is too weak for a V6 torque) and has been happily transplanted into a Getrag/Muncie 4 speed living with a tricked out 3.4 for several years now. Downside: at 60 or 70 mph your engine is screaming at almost 4000 rpm. Not fun on long trips. Great on the street.||||reg||4
